# Digital Maturity Framework for Hospitals

Digital health maturity varies widely across hospitals.
This framework helps assess current state and define a realistic roadmap.

## Level 1 – Foundational
- Basic IT infrastructure (network, servers, backups)
- Standalone HIS / billing systems
- Limited data governance
- High manual dependency

## Level 2 – Operational
- EMR/HMIS adoption in core departments
- PACS/LIS/RIS operational
- Role-based access controls
- Basic reporting and dashboards

## Level 3 – Integrated
- Interoperability between EMR, LIS, PACS
- Clinical workflows digitized
- Data quality monitoring
- Telemedicine and patient engagement tools

## Level 4 – Intelligent
- Analytics-driven decision making
- Registries and longitudinal patient data
- AI/ML used in assistive clinical workflows
- Continuous quality improvement

## Key Principle
Hospitals should progress **sequentially**, not skip levels.
